# The `hyperv` variant (scripts/build-kernel.sh x86_64 OUT hyperv): Hyper-V's clocks, for a
# guest of a Windows host, which runs it in a Windows Hypervisor Platform partition (D140).
# The partition offers Hyper-V's synthetic features, and so the hypervisor's leaves; Linux
# 6.18 marks the TSC unstable on a Hyper-V that does not offer TSC invariance (0x40000003
# EAX bit 15, which no runner of PM M197-M198 offered; arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mshyperv.c), and
# only CONFIG_HYPERV brings the reference TSC page it keeps time by in the TSC's place
# (drivers/clocksource/hyperv_timer.c, CONFIG_HYPERV_TIMER). Not in the kernel KVM and HVF
# guests boot, which would carry Hyper-V's code and use none of it.
CONFIG_HYPERV=y
CONFIG_HYPERV_TIMER=y
# A partition's devices are shards' own, on virtio-mmio: no VMBus, nor its drivers.
# CONFIG_HYPERV_VMBUS is not set
# Interrupt remapping for x2APIC, which the partition's emulated APICs do not offer (M198).
# CONFIG_HYPERV_IOMMU is not set
